# The repo root is the extra build context named "repo", which core's Dockerfile builds
# the docs site from. That build checks that every repo path a page links to exists, so
# every top-level entry git tracks comes in whole; anything else at the root stays out.
*
!.claude-plugin
!.cursor-plugin
!.github
!CITATION.cff
!CLA.md
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!LICENSE
!README.md
!TERMS.md
!THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
!app
!assets
!core
!docker-compose.yml
!docs
!docs-server
!infra
!pyproject.toml
!seeder
!tests

# Local caches, build output and secrets, at any depth.
**/.env
**/*.tfvars
**/*.tfstate*
**/.terraform
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
docs-server/site
